- Encodes current time (milliseconds since epoch) into the first 10 characters using Crockford's Base32[0m[0m
- Detects when the timestamp hasn't changed between calls ("same" flag) and increments the random portion instead of regenerating it, preserving monotonic ordering within the same millisecond[0m[0m
- Handles overflow of the random part (all [38;5;10mZ[0ms) by sleeping ~1.2ms and retrying[0m[0m
- Generates 16 random bytes via [38;5;10mrand[0m crate for the random portion when timestamp changes[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1m[38;5;10msrc/ulidgen.rs[0m — [38;5;10mmain()[0m[22m[0m[0m
- Parses [38;5;10m-n N[0m and [38;5;10m-t[0m flags from argv (matching C's [38;5;10mgetopt[0m behavior)[0m[0m
- In default mode: generates N ULIDs and prints them[0m[0m
- In [38;5;10m-t[0m mode: reads stdin line-by-line and prefixes each with a ULID[0m[0m
